{"ts":"2026-08-15T10:41:12.886Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_instance":"217bde283203d510dd91ecae","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Verified live evidence\n\nAt main 996313a99bf7df942111cac40b8ada53107dcfe5:\n\n- pm contracts --json --full returns only output_budget_exceeded and read_output.\n- output_budget_exceeded.omitted_result is true and reason is requested_budget_infeasible.\n- pm --output-budget unbounded contracts --json --full returns 26 top-level keys, 131 commands, and 104 actions.\n\n## Contract decision required\n\nThe implementation must distinguish three cases:\n\n1. explicit complete-result intent with no explicit budget: completeness wins;\n2. explicit caller budget: the caller's cost ceiling wins and any omission is disclosed;\n3. whole-result omission: this is a failed read, not a successful bounded projection, and must not be parseable as plausible domain data.\n\nThis rule belongs in the shared SDK read-output primitive, not as a contracts-only bypass.\n\n## Regression lineage\n\nGH-1012 and the closed resumability lineage fixed complete-result handling on list-all. The same semantic class now appears on contracts --full, proving the behavior needs a cross-surface invariant."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-2qvq7a"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1030: contracts --json --full is wholly omitted by the default output budget"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The explicit complete-contract request pm contracts --json --full deterministically returns only a well-formed output-budget receipt under the default budget. Because stdout remains valid JSON and the actual contract is wholly omitted, downstream consumers can silently interpret missing command/action arrays as empty and publish structurally valid but content-free artifacts."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":0},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","contracts","full-projection","github-1030","json","output-budget","sdk-contract","silent-data-loss"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-15T10:41:12.886Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-15T10:41:12.886Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":300},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Reproduce the exact contracts failure in SDK and CLI tests; define an SDK-native precedence rule where explicit complete-result intent defeats an implicit default ceiling while explicit caller budgets still win; make any unavoidable omitted_result=true outcome parser-visible through deterministic nonzero exit and transport semantics; apply the class-wide rule to CLI, SDK, and MCP; add negative controls for bounded partial degradation versus whole-result omission; manually verify packed npm, npx, Bun, and bunx consumers in temporary directories; document recovery and compatibility."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Make explicit whole-result reads semantically complete and make whole-result omission impossible to confuse with successful empty data."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Contract generators and agents can trust that --full means complete without carrying command-specific budget folklore."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Downstream docs and integrations can silently regenerate zero-command artifacts while JSON parsing and process health remain green."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"Whole-result intent precedence and omitted_result failure semantics are enforced once in the SDK read-output layer and regression-gated across every complete-result surface."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"The regression is present in the current immutable daily release and has already produced an externally visible zero-command documentation artifact according to GitHub #1030."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5t33or"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"critical"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"critical"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"Reproduced on repository main 996313a99bf7df942111cac40b8ada53107dcfe5 and pm-cli 2026.8.15; Linux; default output budget"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Run pm contracts --json --full and inspect top-level keys. Observe only output_budget_exceeded and read_output with omitted_result=true. Run pm --output-budget unbounded contracts --json --full and observe the complete contract payload."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"An explicit --full whole-surface read returns the complete contract by default, or fails in a parser-visible way before a consumer can mistake a well-formed receipt for an empty contract. CLI, SDK, and MCP expose one precedence rule and one failure contract."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The default invocation returns a successful, parseable JSON receipt with the entire result omitted. Live repository reproduction returned two receipt keys; the unbounded recovery returned 26 top-level keys, 131 commands, and 104 actions."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-8nev0o","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-15T10:41:12.886Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-jt8aa2","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-15T10:41:12.886Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-s2h0mq","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-15T10:41:12.886Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-x0iv17","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-15T10:41:12.886Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-15T10:41:12.886Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate-check evidence 2026-08-15: all-status searches for contracts --json --full,omitted_result,requested_budget_infeasible,JSON.parse,and GitHub #1030 found no item for this current command-path regression. Open parent pm-5t33or owns the universal budget contract; closed pm-8nev0o,pm-jt8aa2,pm-x0iv17,and pm-s2h0mq provide completed resumability,omission-receipt,full-projection,and default-ceiling lineage. This issue records the newly reproduced cross-surface gap without reopening or duplicating those items."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"f5b9e8fd3ace96d71a5fcac1fae819233f940d366ad5d3901b8f9a929674560f","item_hash_version":2,"message":""}
